Subject: [PATCH 02775/11362] [outer-loop] .410 A2 validated the example-corpus
 thesis but was quarantined on a substrate false-positive

exp4433 transferred ka59's grounded win-rule to SOLVE g50t L1 (offline_reproduced, +1 level) -- the
FIRST example-corpus generic-transfer solve, exactly the .410 thesis -- but the artifact wrote
inference_substrate=None so adversarial_verify applied the strict 60s floor -> DURATION_TOO_SHORT
quarantine. Refined the root cause: inference_substrate must be AGENT-EMITTED (a REQUIRED ARTIFACT
FIELD), not just a task-YAML field; a fast deterministic predicate-transfer is verifier-scoring/
aggregation (1s/100us floor), not live_llm_inference. exp4437 (queued) must enforce agent-emission;
the .410 capstone should treat exp4433's g50t solve as a real-but-quarantined corrigendum (thesis
validated); the .411 planner must list inference_substrate in REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS. Did NOT edit
the running roadmap or artifact (no mid-run risk, no gate-gaming).

